From: Hazel Smith <hazel@hazelesque.uk>
Subject: setup_deps.bzl: drop install_python_deps()

Mirrors the WORKSPACE patch — @python_deps is gone, so its
install_deps() and the loads that produce it must go too.
Without this, .bzl evaluation fails before bazel even gets to
the build graph.

diff --git a/setup_deps.bzl b/setup_deps.bzl
index 85d0e63..54435c7 100644
--- a/setup_deps.bzl
+++ b/setup_deps.bzl
@@ -3,9 +3,21 @@ load("@com_github_nelhage_rules_boost//:boost/boost.bzl", "boost_deps")
 load("@hedron_compile_commands//:workspace_setup.bzl", "hedron_compile_commands_setup")
 load("@llvm-raw//utils/bazel:configure.bzl", "llvm_configure")
 load("@com_google_protobuf//:protobuf_deps.bzl", "protobuf_deps")
-load("@python_3_10//:defs.bzl", "interpreter")
-load("@rules_python//python:pip.bzl", "pip_parse")
-load("@python_deps//:requirements.bzl", install_python_deps = "install_deps")
+
+# LOCAL PATCH (Chimera / Python 3.13): upstream also loads
+# `@python_3_10//:defs.bzl` + `@python_deps//:requirements.bzl` +
+# calls `install_python_deps()`.  Stripped here because:
+#
+#   1. @python_3_10 tries to download a glibc-targeted Python
+#      which doesn't run on Chimera's musl libc.
+#   2. pip_parse's vendored pip is incompatible with Python 3.13
+#      (removed `pkgutil.ImpImporter`) — and trying to point it at
+#      an older system python requires having one installed, which
+#      Chimera doesn't default to.
+#
+# Net effect: //tools py_binary targets (reformat_python, analyze_pp_trace,
+# refresh_compile_commands) are unavailable, but //indexer:scip-clang
+# itself has no Python deps and builds fine.
 
 def setup_dependencies():
     bazel_skylib_workspace()
@@ -17,5 +29,3 @@ def setup_dependencies():
     llvm_configure(name = "llvm-project", targets = ["AArch64", "X86"])
 
     protobuf_deps()
-
-    install_python_deps()
